{% set nmi = hookable_metadata.context.nmi %}

{#
    Only rendered when the store has said this payment opens recurring charges: the card is kept so
    that the store can charge it again, later and without the shopper present, for payments that do
    not exist yet. The shopper is told so before paying, in words of its own — neither the option to
    save a card for next time, which this payment does not offer, nor the note that an order will be
    charged later.

    The default wording is neutral on purpose. What a store actually commits to — how often, how the
    amount is set, how to stop it — is its own, and it says so by translating this key.
#}
{% if nmi.recurring_charges|default(false) %}
    <p class="alert alert-info" {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('nmi-recurring-commitment') }}>
        {{ 'jpm_martin_sylius_nmi.shop.pay.recurring_commitment'|trans }}
    </p>
{% endif %}
